  { type: "h", text: "3. In front, on both sides" },
  {
    type: "p",
    md: `The inverse goes **in front** of each side. That is called pre-multiplying, and it matters because $AB$ and $BA$ are different matrices.\nWriting $A^{-1}$ in front on one side and behind on the other breaks the equation, and it is the slip the examiners look for here. One rule covers every question on this specification: inverse first, both sides.`,
  },
